Johns Hopkins Turbulence Databases — numerical flow evidence (@fd-jhtdb: 0, is #reference, #part-of @fd-sources) { r_1D25T86CC1CHT4BX098WQXBQPE
Johns Hopkins Turbulence Databases. [Current database-access portal](https://turbulence.idies.jhu.edu/database) · [Legacy portal and migration notices](https://turbulence.pha.jhu.edu/?legacy=1).

Read the selected simulation's governing equations, forcing, geometry, resolution, time range, interpolation/differentiation methods and citation instructions before extracting a statistic. Reproduce a known result, then vary sample duration, spacing and estimator. These are numerical experiments with declared models, not measurements of an arbitrary physical flow.

The current portal permits small testing requests below 4,096 points with a public testing identifier; larger work requires an authorization token requested from the project. The legacy page reports HTTP-to-HTTPS problems in older SOAP/pyJHTDB tools and directs users to new Python/Matlab access methods. Access conditions and dataset terms should be checked at use. No token request, data retrieval or copied dataset is part of this Record.

**Return:** [Fluid dynamics sources — books, courses, methods and physical evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_3Y3TVV9VQAB50M2ZSECK5JTYVG).
